   "he": "נָפַל לְפָנָיו כּוּ׳. אָמַר רַב: ״לְפָנָיו״ – לְפָנָיו מַמָּשׁ, ״לְאַחֲרָיו״ – אַחֲרָיו מַמָּשׁ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If a man was digging or widening a pit, and an ox passing by «fell forward» into it in fright due to the sound of the digging, he is liable. If it fell backward into the pit due to the sound of the digging, he is exempt. «Rav says:» The term «forward» means «literally forward,» and the term «backward» means «literally backward,»"
  }
